pve-tools (1.10.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * pve-sdn-healthcheck 1.1.0: add --drop-window / SDN_DROP_WINDOW and
    report active rx/tx dropped-packet deltas over one shared sample window
    for all live NICs, avoiding per-NIC sleeps while preserving accurate
    multi-interface figures.

 -- Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte+software@gmail.com>  Fri, 03 Jul 2026 11:42:00 -0400

pve-tools (1.9.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * pve-sdn-healthcheck 1.0.1: fix mtu_local false positive when the
    VXLAN carrier is a jumbo parent bridge (for example vmbr0) but route
    lookup to a VTEP selects a 1500-byte host service VLAN subinterface
    (for example vmbr0.$VLANTAG).

 -- Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte+software@gmail.com>  Fri, 03 Jul 2026 11:24:00 -0400

pve-tools (1.9.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New tools:
    - pve-rolling-upgrade 1.0.0 - rolling, health-gated PVE 8->9 node
      upgrade: live-migrate guests off (HA-aware), dist-upgrade
      bookworm->trixie, pin NIC names, reboot, and gate on Ceph
      active+clean / quorum / EVPN before moving on. Hard-stops on any
      failed gate.
    - pve-ceph-upgrade 1.0.0 - online Ceph major-release migration
      (e.g. squid->tentacle): stage packages, then restart
      mon->mgr->osd->mds gating on health, then require-osd-release.
  * pve-import-cloud-images 1.4.0: version-aware, migration-safe CPU
    baseline selection.
  * pve-sdn-healthcheck: detect and opt-in fix for a stale zebra ZAPI
    socket that causes L3-VNI black-holes.
  * Bundled tool versions: pve-import-cloud-images 1.4.0,
    pve-vmnic-fix 1.0.0, pve-create-tshoot-image 1.3.0,
    pve-sdn-healthcheck 1.0.0, pve-rolling-upgrade 1.0.0,
    pve-ceph-upgrade 1.0.0.

 -- Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte+software@gmail.com>  Tue, 16 Jun 2026 20:36:32 -0300

pve-tools (1.8.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release published as a Debian package via the openSUSE Build
    Service, as an alternative to the manual copy procedure. Bundled tools:
    - pve-import-cloud-images 1.3.0
    - pve-vmnic-fix 1.0.0
    - pve-create-tshoot-image 1.3.0
    - pve-sdn-healthcheck 1.0.0 (new since 1.7.0)
  * Install scripts to /usr/sbin, man pages to /usr/share/man/man8,
    and bash completion to /usr/share/bash-completion/completions.

